# `Object.defineProperty(P.prototype, "shown", { get() { .. } })`: the row says which operand is the key, and a text is written there. So the definition lies under that name, as one of a written map does.
# The layout of P, off which only `x` is read, keeps its proofs. That of Q escapes once a lookup under the name comes by. A key that is no written text is any key: R.
# RUN: summary f0
# CHECK: change {{*}}DefinesByDescriptor {{*}}"shown"
# CHECK: change {{*}}DefinesByDescriptor {{*}}"shown"
# RUN(LINK): link fields layouts mechanisms=all
# LINK: field L0.0 "x" proven=i32 writers-known
